    "# Repository Functional Test Intelligence\n\n"
    "Analyze the supplied component using the indexed project and workspace.\n\n"
    + mcp_instruction +
    "\n\n## Runtime Inputs\n\n"
    "PROJECT ID:\n"
    + project_id +
    "\n\nWORKSPACE_ROOT:\n"
    + workspace_path +
    "\n\n## Objective\n\n"
    "Produce a complete evidence-backed functional test intelligence baseline.\n\n"
    "The required analysis consists of:\n"
    "1. Expected functional scenario discovery\n"
    "2. Executable functional test discovery\n"
    "3. Test-to-scenario mapping\n"
    "4. Functional scenario mapping\n"
    "5. Unmapped test identification\n"
    "6. Dependency evidence\n"
    "7. Test classification\n\n"
    "## Execution Order\n\n"
    "Perform the analysis in this order and do not skip a step:\n"
    "1. Retrieve application entry points from MCP/indexed data and derive the expected functional scenarios (see Functional Scenario Rules).\n"
    "2. Discover every executable in-scope test in WORKSPACE_ROOT (see Test Scope). Do not sample and do not stop at the first files found.\n"
    "3. For each test, retrieve dependency evidence from MCP/indexed graph data (see Dependency Rule).\n"
    "4. Map each test to scenarios (see Mapping Rules), then derive each scenario's status and mapped_test_case_ids from the test mappings.\n"
    "5. Classify each test (see Classification).\n"
    "6. Build all records in the required order, then compute the metrics by counting the records you built.\n"
    "7. Run the Final Consistency Checks. Return the JSON only after every check passes.\n\n"
    "## Available Skills\n\n"
    "Use the available specialized skills through `invoke_skill` when their detailed methodology is required.\n"
    "Do not reproduce skill instructions manually.\n"
    "If a skill's output format differs from the Required JSON Output section, the Required JSON Output section governs.\n"
    "If `invoke_skill` is unavailable or fails, continue with the rules in this prompt and record the failure in `limitations`.\n\n"
    "## Source Rules\n\n"
    "MCP/indexed data is the primary source for:\n"
    "- indexed project information\n"
    "- application symbols\n"
    "- relationships\n"
    "- dependency graph\n"
    "- query graph\n"
    "- API/application entry points\n"
    "- source references\n\n"
    "WORKSPACE_ROOT is the source for:\n"
    "- source files\n"
    "- test files\n"
    "- configuration\n"
    "- files unavailable through MCP\n"
    "- exact test definitions\n\n"
    "Do not load the entire repository or entire dependency graph.\n"
    "Retrieve targeted evidence.\n"
    "Reuse evidence already obtained.\n\n"
    "## Dependency Rule\n\n"
    "Do not generate a dependency graph with the LLM.\n\n"
    "Retrieve dependency information from MCP/indexed graph data.\n"
    "Use the traversal depth stated in the MCP instructions above. If none is stated, use the MCP tool's default.\n"
    "Record each dependency path exactly as returned by MCP/indexed graph data. Do not add inferred edges or inferred nodes.\n\n"
    "For each test, attempt to establish:\n"
    "- test entry point\n"
    "- application entry point\n"
    "- application symbol\n"
    "- dependency path\n\n"
    "Static dependency relationships are structural evidence only.\n"
    "Do not claim that every statically connected dependency definitely executed at runtime.\n\n"
    "## Functional Scenario Rules\n\n"
    "A functional scenario is a distinct externally observable application behavior.\n\n"
    "Do not create one scenario per:\n"
    "- class\n"
    "- method\n"
    "- repository\n"
    "- database query\n"
    "- helper\n"
    "- internal service call\n\n"
    "unless that element itself represents distinct externally observable functionality.\n\n"
    "### Scenario Derivation\n\n"
    "Derive scenarios only from application entry points returned by MCP/indexed data and from source evidence for those entry points.\n"
    "Never derive a scenario from a test name, test file or feature file.\n"
    "Create one scenario per application entry point.\n"
    "Create an additional scenario for the same entry point only when source evidence shows a distinct externally observable outcome, such as a distinct response status, error response or behavior branch implemented for that entry point. Cite that evidence.\n"
    "Do not invent entry points.\n\n"
    "### Identifiers\n\n"
    "scenario_id = \"SCN:\" + entry point identifier\n"
    "For an additional outcome scenario, append \"#\" + outcome slug (lowercase words joined by hyphens).\n"
    "Entry point identifier = \"<HTTP method> <route>\" for HTTP entry points, otherwise the fully qualified symbol name. Use the exact spelling returned by MCP/indexed data.\n"
    "test_case_id = framework + \":\" + path relative to WORKSPACE_ROOT (forward slashes) + \"::\" + test name + \"@L\" + start_line\n"
    "Identifiers must be identical across runs for identical source.\n\n"
    "### Ordering\n\n"
    "Sort functional_scenarios by scenario_id and test_cases by test_case_id, ascending, in plain code-point order.\n"
    "Sort every array of strings the same way. Sort evidence items by type, then value.\n\n"
    "## Test Scope\n\n"
    "Count ONLY executable:\n"
    "- Karate\n"
    "- Playwright\n"
    "- Selenium\n\n"
    "Do not count:\n"
    "- unit tests\n"
    "- JUnit-only tests\n"
    "- TestNG-only tests\n"
    "- test files\n"
    "- feature files as containers\n"
    "- test classes as containers\n"
    "- fixtures\n"
    "- hooks\n"
    "- step definitions\n"
    "- page objects\n"
    "- helpers\n\n"
    "JUnit-only and TestNG-only mean tests that use none of Karate, Playwright or Selenium.\n"
    "A Selenium test qualifies only when it is an executable test declaration (a test method or function run by the test framework) that uses Selenium WebDriver APIs directly or through page objects or helpers, as shown by source or MCP/indexed evidence.\n\n"
    "### Test Granularity\n\n"
    "Karate:\n"
    "Each executable Scenario is one logical test case.\n\n"
    "Playwright:\n"
    "Each executable test declaration is one test case.\n\n"
    "Selenium:\n"
    "Each qualifying executable functional test method is one test case.\n\n"
    "Do not multiply parameterized tests unless deterministic framework/parser evidence identifies generated executable cases.\n\n"
    "## Mapping Rules\n\n"
    "Every test has exactly one mapping.status:\n"
    "- \"mapped\": evidence connects the test to the application entry point of the scenario (from MCP/indexed dependency evidence or the test's own source) and, for an outcome scenario, evidence shows the test asserts that outcome. mapping.scenario_ids lists every scenario the test is mapped to.\n"
    "- \"ambiguous\": evidence connects the test to an application entry point but does not establish which scenario it exercises (for example the asserted outcome cannot be identified). mapping.scenario_ids lists the candidate scenarios.\n"
    "- \"unmapped\": sufficient evidence was retrieved and it shows the test exercises no expected scenario. mapping.scenario_ids is empty.\n"
    "- \"insufficient_evidence\": the evidence needed to decide could not be retrieved. mapping.scenario_ids is empty.\n\n"
    "Every scenario has exactly one status:\n"
    "- \"covered\": covered according to the Coverage Definition.\n"
    "- \"uncertain\": not covered, and at least one test with mapping.status \"ambiguous\" lists it in mapping.scenario_ids.\n"
    "- \"uncovered\": not covered and not listed by any ambiguous test.\n\n"
    "mapped_test_case_ids of a scenario contains only tests whose mapping.status is \"mapped\" and whose mapping.scenario_ids include that scenario.\n\n"
    "## Coverage Definition\n\n"
    "A functional scenario is covered ONLY when at least one in-scope test has:\n\n"
    "mapping.status = \"mapped\"\n\n"
    "and lists that scenario in mapping.scenario_ids.\n\n"
    "The following do not count as coverage:\n"
    "- ambiguous\n"
    "- unmapped\n"
    "- insufficient_evidence\n\n"
    "Formula:\n\n"
    "coverage_percent = covered_functional_scenarios / expected_functional_scenarios * 100, rounded to 2 decimal places, as a JSON number.\n\n"
    "If expected_functional_scenarios = 0:\n\n"
    "coverage_percent = null\n\n"
    "## Required Metrics\n\n"
    "Return:\n\n"
    "- expected_functional_scenarios\n"
    "- covered_functional_scenarios\n"
    "- coverage_percent\n"
    "- total_test_cases\n"
    "- mapped_test_cases\n"
    "- unmapped_test_cases\n\n"
    "Definitions:\n\n"
    "expected_functional_scenarios = number of records in functional_scenarios\n\n"
    "covered_functional_scenarios = number of scenarios whose status is \"covered\"\n\n"
    "total_test_cases = number of records in test_cases\n\n"
    "mapped_test_cases = number of test cases whose mapping.status is \"mapped\"\n\n"
    "unmapped_test_cases = number of test cases whose mapping.status is \"unmapped\"\n\n"
    "Ambiguous and insufficient_evidence tests must remain explicitly represented.\n"
    "Do not silently convert them to unmapped.\n"
    "They are counted in total_test_cases only, so total_test_cases can be greater than mapped_test_cases + unmapped_test_cases.\n\n"
    "## Required Complete Records\n\n"
    "Return EVERY expected functional scenario.\n"
    "Return EVERY executable in-scope test case.\n"
    "Do not return only summaries.\n"
    "Every record contains every field listed below. Use [], null or 0 instead of omitting a field.\n\n"
    "Every functional scenario must contain:\n"
    "- scenario_id\n"
    "- name\n"
    "- description\n"
    "- status\n"
    "- mapped_test_case_ids\n"
    "- evidence\n\n"
    "Every test case must contain:\n"
    "- test_case_id\n"
    "- framework\n"
    "- name\n"
    "- source\n"
    "- mapping\n"
    "- dependency\n"
    "- classification\n\n"
    "## Classification\n\n"
    "Evaluate every test for:\n"
    "- smoke\n"
    "- regression\n"
    "- e2e\n\n"
    "Evaluate every test for:\n"
    "- Critical\n"
    "- Medium\n"
    "- Low\n\n"
    "Multiple labels are allowed.\n"
    "Every positive label requires evidence.\n"
    "Accepted evidence for a label: a test tag, an annotation, suite configuration, pipeline configuration, or a dependency path recorded in the same test record.\n"
    "Critical, Medium and Low require an explicit tag, annotation, suite configuration or pipeline configuration that states that level. Never derive them from a name, a path or dependency depth.\n"
    "When no label is supported by evidence, use an empty labels array and describe what could not be established in unknowns.\n"
    "Do not invent business criticality.\n\n"
    "## Evidence\n\n"
    "Every important conclusion must have concise evidence.\n\n"
    "Each evidence item is an object with a \"type\" and a \"value\". \"type\" is exactly one of:\n"
    "- source\n"
    "- repository\n"
    "- path\n"
    "- line_range\n"
    "- symbol\n"
    "- api_route\n"
    "- dependency_path\n"
    "- test_tag\n"
    "- annotation\n"
    "- pipeline_configuration\n"
    "- suite_configuration\n"
    "- explanation\n\n"
    "\"value\" is one short string.\n\n"
    "Filename or name alone is weak evidence.\n"
    "Do not fabricate evidence.\n\n"
    "## Uncertainty\n\n"
    "Use explicit states rather than guessing:\n"
    "- functional scenario status: covered, uncovered, uncertain\n"
    "- test mapping.status: mapped, ambiguous, unmapped, insufficient_evidence\n"
    "- analysis_status: complete, partial, failure\n\n"
    "Do not resolve an uncertain state by guessing.\n\n"
    "## Required JSON Output\n\n"
    "Return exactly one JSON object.\n"
    "The final message must contain only that object: no text before or after it, no Markdown code fence, no comments and no trailing commas.\n"
    "Use double quotes. Escape backslashes and quotes inside strings. Numeric fields are JSON numbers, never strings.\n\n"
    "How to read the template below:\n"
    "- a|b|c lists the allowed values. Write exactly one of them and never the \"|\" character.\n"
    "- <integer>, <integer_or_null> and <number_or_null> stand for a real JSON number (or null where the name says so).\n"
    "- <string_or_null> stands for a real JSON string or null.\n"
    "- \"<string>\" stands for a real string.\n"
    "- an array shows the shape of one element. Return one element per record, or [] when there are none.\n"
    "- never copy a template value literally.\n\n"
    "{\n"
    "  \"analysis_status\": \"complete|partial|failure\",\n"
    "  \"project\": {\n"
    "    \"project_id\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "    \"workspace_root\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "    \"index_status\": <string_or_null>\n"
    "  },\n"
    "  \"metrics\": {\n"
    "    \"expected_functional_scenarios\": <integer>,\n"
    "    \"covered_functional_scenarios\": <integer>,\n"
    "    \"coverage_percent\": <number_or_null>,\n"
    "    \"total_test_cases\": <integer>,\n"
    "    \"mapped_test_cases\": <integer>,\n"
    "    \"unmapped_test_cases\": <integer>\n"
    "  },\n"
    "  \"functional_scenarios\": [\n"
    "    {\n"
    "      \"scenario_id\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "      \"name\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "      \"description\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "      \"status\": \"covered|uncovered|uncertain\",\n"
    "      \"mapped_test_case_ids\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "      \"evidence\": [{\"type\": \"<evidence type>\", \"value\": \"<string>\"}]\n"
    "    }\n"
    "  ],\n"
    "  \"test_cases\": [\n"
    "    {\n"
    "      \"test_case_id\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "      \"name\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "      \"framework\": \"karate|playwright|selenium\",\n"
    "      \"source\": {\n"
    "        \"path\": \"<string>\",\n"
    "        \"start_line\": <integer_or_null>,\n"
    "        \"end_line\": <integer_or_null>\n"
    "      },\n"
    "      \"mapping\": {\n"
    "        \"status\": \"mapped|unmapped|ambiguous|insufficient_evidence\",\n"
    "        \"scenario_ids\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "        \"evidence\": [{\"type\": \"<evidence type>\", \"value\": \"<string>\"}]\n"
    "      },\n"
    "      \"dependency\": {\n"
    "        \"entry_points\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "        \"services\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "        \"components\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "        \"external_systems\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "        \"dependency_paths\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "        \"max_depth\": <integer>,\n"
    "        \"boundaries_crossed\": <integer>\n"
    "      },\n"
    "      \"classification\": {\n"
    "        \"labels\": [\"<label>\"],\n"
    "        \"evidence\": [{\"type\": \"<evidence type>\", \"value\": \"<string>\"}],\n"
    "        \"unknowns\": [\"<string>\"]\n"
    "      }\n"
    "    }\n"
    "  ],\n"
    "  \"uncovered_scenarios\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "  \"unmapped_test_cases\": [\"<string>\"],\n"
    "  \"limitations\": [\"<string>\"]\n"
    "}\n\n"
    "Field rules:\n"
    "- project.project_id: copy the PROJECT ID from Runtime Inputs exactly, as a JSON string.\n"
    "- project.workspace_root: copy the WORKSPACE_ROOT from Runtime Inputs exactly, as a JSON string. Escape backslashes.\n"
    "- project.index_status: the index status reported by MCP/indexed data for this project, copied as reported. Use null if none was reported.\n"
    "- source.path: path relative to WORKSPACE_ROOT, with forward slashes.\n"
    "- source.start_line and source.end_line: 1-based and inclusive, covering the test declaration (Karate Scenario or Scenario Outline block, Playwright test declaration, Selenium test method). Use null and add a limitation if they cannot be determined.\n"
    "- dependency.entry_points, services, components, external_systems: identifiers exactly as returned by MCP/indexed data. Use [] when none were retrieved.\n"
    "- dependency.dependency_paths: one string per path, with node identifiers joined by \" -> \" in traversal order, starting at the test entry point.\n"
    "- dependency.max_depth: the largest number of \" -> \" separators in any dependency path. 0 when there are no paths.\n"
    "- dependency.boundaries_crossed: the number of distinct consecutive node pairs, across all dependency paths, whose second node is listed in external_systems. 0 when there are none.\n"
    "- classification.labels: zero or more of exactly: smoke, regression, e2e, Critical, Medium, Low.\n"
    "- uncovered_scenarios: the scenario_id of every scenario whose status is \"uncovered\". Do not include \"uncertain\" scenarios.\n"
    "- unmapped_test_cases: the test_case_id of every test whose mapping.status is \"unmapped\". Do not include \"ambiguous\" or \"insufficient_evidence\" tests.\n"
    "- limitations: one string per limitation. Use [] when there are none.\n"
    "- analysis_status \"complete\": every record was produced, no test has mapping.status \"insufficient_evidence\" and every consistency check passed.\n"
    "- analysis_status \"partial\": evidence was missing (including any \"insufficient_evidence\" test, a failed MCP query or a failed skill call). Still return every record you could build.\n"
    "- analysis_status \"failure\": MCP/indexed data for this PROJECT ID was unavailable, so no analysis could be performed. Return empty arrays, zero metrics, coverage_percent null, and explain in limitations.\n\n"
    "## Final Consistency Checks\n\n"
    "Before returning the JSON, verify:\n\n"
    "1. functional_scenarios.length == metrics.expected_functional_scenarios\n"
    "2. test_cases.length == metrics.total_test_cases\n"
    "3. Number of scenarios with at least one mapped test == number of scenarios with status \"covered\" == metrics.covered_functional_scenarios\n"
    "4. Number of tests with mapping.status == \"mapped\" == metrics.mapped_test_cases\n"
    "5. Number of tests with mapping.status == \"unmapped\" == metrics.unmapped_test_cases\n"
    "6. Every test has a classification object.\n"
    "7. Every mapped or ambiguous mapping has evidence.\n"
    "8. Every positive classification has evidence.\n"
    "9. Every dependency path originates from MCP/indexed evidence.\n"
    "10. No feature file or test file is counted as a test case merely because it exists.\n"
    "11. No class or method is counted as a functional scenario merely because it exists.\n"
    "12. No missing information is replaced with an invented conclusion.\n"
    "13. scenario_id values are unique, and test_case_id values are unique.\n"
    "14. Every id in mapped_test_case_ids, mapping.scenario_ids, uncovered_scenarios and unmapped_test_cases exists in functional_scenarios or test_cases.\n"
    "15. For every scenario, mapped_test_case_ids equals the ids of the tests whose mapping.status is \"mapped\" and whose mapping.scenario_ids include that scenario.\n"
    "16. uncovered_scenarios equals the scenarios with status \"uncovered\", and unmapped_test_cases equals the tests with mapping.status \"unmapped\".\n"
    "17. coverage_percent equals the Formula rounded to 2 decimal places, and is null only when expected_functional_scenarios is 0.\n"
    "18. Every enumerated field holds exactly one allowed value and none contains \"|\".\n"
    "19. All arrays follow the Ordering rules.\n"
    "20. analysis_status matches the Field rules.\n"
    "21. The output is one valid JSON object.\n\n"
    "If a check fails, correct the records and recompute the metrics from them. Never change a metric to match records that are wrong.\n\n"
    "If the analysis cannot be completed because evidence is missing, set:\n\n"
    "analysis_status = \"partial\"\n\n"
    "and explain the limitation in `limitations`.\n\n"
    "Do not omit records merely because evidence is incomplete.\n"
)
